<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico completes secondary operations.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico placed all three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements it had offered in order to drain 1.595 billion pesos from the secondary market on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    360 days   20.66 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    178 days   20.40 pct</p>
<p>    150 million     87 days   19.26 pct</p>
<p>The amounts and maturities of the repurchase agreements were assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    500 million     49 days   20.00 pct</p>
<p>    500 million     17 days   19.75 pct</p>
<p>    145 million	1 day    19.00 pct</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>(( --Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9559))</p>
</text>
